**Resubmitted: T4C — deviation, preferred-level redline at §14.2.2 (validated ok:true).**

Change made in response to the verifier's failed "Customer convenience termination present" check: the operative grant now reads "PB may terminate this Agreement **for convenience, without cause, at any time** upon thirty (30) days' prior written notice to SFJ" — the convenience/without-cause character is now unmistakable on the face of the operative language rather than inferable from the section heading.

All four preferred elements remain carried by the single replace:
1. Unconditional PB convenience right (gating $60M spend threshold and pre-approval window deleted);
2. Thirty (30) days' prior written notice (blank [***] resolved);
3. Pro rata refund of PB prepayments;
4. Express bar on SFJ convenience termination during the Term.

Minimality holds (57 words in, 41 out); the 300% Trial Data Package buy-out, ARTICLE 6 Approval Payment carry-over and Section 6.2 adjustment are retained verbatim. Residual commercial points — the exit is unconditional but not free, and §14.2.10's JSC-disagreement right is near-discretionary — are flagged in the rationale for negotiation rather than by a second redline.
